       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen is a toxic dose. It is well above the 3,200 mg/day ceiling, and I know of no indication where it would help. At that dose, serious harm is likely for a patient with normal kidney and liver function. That includes GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the labeled range right away, such as 800 mg PO three times daily or 600 mg PO four times daily.\n- Help you consider other options if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. Examples are scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen, or other agents.\n- Leave the order for pharmacy or a second prescriber to review if you think there's a special circumstance I'm missing. They can enter it through their own verification process.\n\nIf you tell me the clinical goal, I can help work out an appropriate order."
